    <string id="SetEndIdle">End game when idle</string>
    <string id="SetEndIdlePrompt">Minutes with no skating detected before the game saves itself, so a recording left running does not carry on for hours. It buzzes first and any button cancels. Set 0 to never end by itself. Anything else is held to 20 minutes or more, because an intermission is 15 to 18 minutes of sitting down and a shorter setting would end a game that is still being played.</string>
    <string id="LabelEndingGame">ENDING GAME</string>
    <string id="SetStrideLength">Stride length (cm)</string>
    <string id="SetStrideLengthPrompt">How far one skating push carries you, in centimetres. Leave at 0 and the app reports stride rate only. Set it and it also reports an estimated distance and on-ice speed - which are only as good as this number, and nothing on the watch can measure it for you. A skating push is typically 260-360 cm, far longer than a walking step.</string>
    <string id="SetUseGps">Use GPS</string>
    <string id="SetUseGpsPrompt">Record speed and distance. Indoor rinks rarely get a fix; outdoor rinks do</string>
